title: The Cabinet
subtitle: Change the policies and the politics of the government.
is-pinned-card: true
card-image: img/cards/cabinet.svg?v=2
tags: advisor
new-page: true
view-if: (in_coalition = 1 and bol_regime = 0) or lsr_in_gov = 1

= The Cabinet

[? if in_coalition = 1 and bol_regime = 0 : The party shares the government, and with it the power to set the country's course. ?][? if lsr_in_gov = 1 and bol_regime = 1 : The party holds a few commissariats in a government that is not its own: the land and the courts are in its hands, and not much else. ?] A change of course takes a turn, and the cabinet cannot change course again for two months. Policies have a lasting effect, month by month.

[? if ant_kad >= 40 : The liberals are in an angry mood. ?][? if ant_gen >= 40 : The generals are muttering about the government. ?][? if ant_bol >= 40 and bol_regime = 0 : Pravda has begun to campaign against the cabinet. ?]Each camp that opposes a policy will first try sanctions, and then, if it is angry enough, take up arms: see the Opposition tab on the right. An unpopular law can be phased in gently, passed by decree, or, if the party is strong enough (its strength is shown there), passed and enforced against its opponents: the odds are shown for each camp, and a failure makes the camp angrier.

Land: [+ pol_land : pol_land +]. [? if in_coalition = 1 and bol_regime = 0 : Food: [+ pol_food : pol_food +]. Finance: [+ pol_finance : pol_finance +]. Labour: [+ pol_labour : pol_labour +]. ?][? if at_war = 1 and in_coalition = 1 and bol_regime = 0 : The war: [+ pol_war : pol_war +]. ?]Order: [+ pol_order : pol_order +].

- @land_0: Leave the land to the Assembly.
- @land_1: Let the land committees regulate the transfers of land.
- @land_2: Socialise the land now, by decree.
- @food_0: Leave the grain trade to the market.
- @food_1: Enforce the grain monopoly and fixed prices.
- @food_2: Send detachments to requisition grain.
- @war_0: Fight a defensive war.
- @war_1: Press for a general peace: Stockholm and the neutrals.
- @war_2: Prepare an offensive with the Allies.
- @order_0: Govern by the ordinary law.
- @order_1: Introduce emergency measures against disorder.
- @order_2: Proclaim broad liberties and an amnesty.
- @finance_0: Pay for the state with the printing press.
- @finance_1: Tax war profits and the rich, and float a Liberty Loan.
- @finance_2: Borrow from the Allies, on their terms.
- @labour_0: Leave industry to the employers.
- @labour_1: Guarantee the eight-hour day and the factory committees.
- @labour_2: Regulate industry through the state.
- @kadets_in: Invite the Kadets back into the government.
- @kadets_out: Dismiss the Kadet ministers and govern with the Soviet parties alone.
- @root: Return to main

@land_0
view-if: (in_coalition = 1 or lsr_in_gov = 1) and pol_land != 0
choose-if: cabinet_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cabinet_timer > 0 : The cabinet has changed course too recently. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.cabinet_timer = 2;
Q.pol_land = 0;
Q.soft_land = 0;
RO.add(Q, {land_pressure: 2, rel_kad: 2});
!}

The land question is left to the Constituent Assembly, as the liberals ask. The peasants are told to be patient.

- @root: Continue.

@land_1
view-if: (in_coalition = 1 or lsr_in_gov = 1) and pol_land != 1
choose-if: cabinet_timer <= 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cabinet_timer > 0 : The cabinet has changed course too recently. ?]

How should it be carried out? Phased in, with compensation and negotiation, it will cost a resource, do less and anger less. By decree it will do all that it says, and its opponents will answer. And a party strong enough can pass it and enforce it against them.

- @land_1_slow: Phase it in, with compensation and negotiation.
- @land_1_decree: Pass it by decree, as written.
- @land_1_force: Pass it by decree, and break any opposition by force.
- @root: Think again.

@land_1_slow
choose-if: resources >= 1
subtitle: Milder effects and little anger. Costs 1 resource.
unavailable-subtitle: We have nothing to pay the compensation with.
on-arrival: {!
Q.month_actions += 1;
Q.cabinet_timer = 2;
Q.pol_land = 1;
Q.soft_land = 1;
RO.law(Q, 'slow', () => {
RO.add(Q, {land_pressure: -4, rel_kad: -3, right_threat: 1, ant_kad: 4, ant_gen: 2}); RO.boost(Q, {peasants: 2}); Q.land_committees = (Q.land_committees || 0) + 1;
}, "Let the land committees regulate the transfers of land");
!}

The land committees now have the government's authority to regulate the transfers until the Assembly meets. (It was phased in, with compensation where it was owed.)

- @root: Continue.

@land_1_decree
subtitle: The law as written. Its opponents will answer.
